// Structures whose picture is chosen by what stands next to them.
//
// One family of `tfs/assets/sprites.ron`'s roster. Every .ron in this
// directory is baked, in FILE-NAME order and then expansion order, so
// the atlas layout is a function of the manifest and not of the
// filesystem. Two files claiming one sprite name is a bake error.
//
// tg draws a row of tables as forty-seven pre-baked frames rather than
// as one picture with a border: an object counts the neighbours it
// belongs with, packs the answer into a byte, and wears
// `"[base_icon_state]-[junction]"` (`code/__HELPERS/icon_smoothing.dm:285`).
// Only 47 of the 256 byte values can be reached, and a sheet carries
// exactly those 47 frames — so `Junctions` bakes the whole family from
// one row rather than making a content author spell out numbers that
// mean nothing to a reader.
//
// The junction a thing is at is the SERVER's arithmetic
// (`crates/lunatic-server/src/structures/smoothing.rs`), which also
// refuses to load any entry whose family is missing a single frame. All
// this file does is put the frames where that check can find them.
(
    sheets: [
        ("table", "obj/smooth_structures/table.dmi"),
    ],
    groups: [
        (
            sheet: "table",
            sprites: [
                Junctions("table", "table"),
            ],
        ),
    ],
)
